  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal legal term. Also written as {棄損|きそん} with a simpler kanji. The compound {名誉|めいよ}{毀損|きそん} (defamation) is the most common usage in modern Japanese and appears frequently in news about lawsuits and online harassment.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {名誉|めいよ}{毀損|きそん}: defamation\n- {器物|きぶつ}{毀損|きそん}: destruction of property\n- {信用|しんよう}{毀損|きそん}: damage to credit/credibility\n- {文書|ぶんしょ}{毀損|きそん}: document destruction",
